<title>JAPAN: Japan PM to visit five ASEAN countries in January.</title>
<headline>Japan PM to visit five ASEAN countries in January.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto will visit five members of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) next month, the government said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Hashimoto would visit Brunei, Malaysia, Indonesia, Vietnam and Singapore from January 7-15 to discuss bilateral and international affairs with their leaders, government spokesman Seiroku Kajiyama told a news conference.</p>
<p>Hashimoto's visit to the region would &quot;reinforce good relations between the countries and Japan,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>ASEAN, which also includes Thailand and the Philippines, marks the 30th anniversary of its founding next year.</p>
<p>At a summit meeting in Jakarta last week, ASEAN said observer nations Burma, Laos and Cambodia would be granted full membership simultaneously it but stopped short of saying when.</p>
</text>
